-- title:
--   Local splitting carrying a maximal order to integral matrices
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $q,q'$ be primes such that the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ShimuraCurve.html#L20), that is: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ which is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb Q$-span is the whole algebra, it is finitely generated, and every submodule with these four properties containing $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ with $q\notin v$ and $q'\notin v$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v\to M_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ such that $\varphi(1\otimes r)=r\cdot 1$ for every $r\in\mathbb Q_v$, and such that, for every $x$ in the tensor product, $x$ lies in the additive subgroup [`Submodule.localBox Λ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ a $v$-adic integer if and only if all four entries $\varphi(x)_{ij}$ are $v$-adic integers.
--
--   This is the local statement that an indefinite rational quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q$ and $q'$ splits at every other finite place, with the splitting isomorphism chosen so that the completion of a maximal order becomes the full matrix algebra over the $v$-adic integers. It is used in the adelic manipulations attached to the Shimura curve of discriminant $qq'$, for instance in the construction of elements of the finite-idele stabiliser of $\Lambda$ with prescribed reduced norm and in the local approximation statements for `localBox`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsMaximalOrder_exists_ringEquiv_mem_localBox_iff_of_isIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt_of_prime.lean

